  "body": "Goal: A Recipes tab shows a tool's speeds and feeds per material. It shows surface speed and feed per tooth, and it can suggest or copy rows.\n\nParent: #3663. Plan: the implementation plan in the #3663 comment. This is PR U5 of 11.\n\nFiles:\n- Add `tool_library_dialog/recipes_tab.rs`. It calls `tool_cutting_rows::cutting_rows`. Do not copy it.\n- Add read-only columns: surface speed `Vc = pi x D x n / 1000` and feed per tooth `fz = F / (n x z)`.\n- Mark the row of the document's material (`cutting::material_of`). Add an \"Add material\" button.\n- \"Copy from tool\" copies the rows of another tool into the draft.\n- \"Suggest\" fills the draft row from the pure table in `crates/tools/src/cutting.rs` (`WorkMaterial::window`, `rpm_for`, `feed_for`). Do not use `ApplyCuttingData`: it acts on an operation, not on a tool row. Apply is `ChangeTool`.\n- The cutting group leaves the property summary.\n\nTests (new): `layout_window_tool_editor` gets the Recipes tab. `tool_library_recipes::suggest_fills_the_draft_and_apply_is_one_undo_step`, `copy_from_tool_copies_the_rows`, `the_document_material_row_is_marked`.\n\nDepends on: U2 (#3893).\n\nCommands: `ChangeTool`. Nothing new. MCP agents already set the same rows with `edit_tool`.\n\nExpected quick gate: 10 steps, if the Suggest helper stays in the UI.\n\nDone means: the Recipes tab lists the rows with Vc and fz. Suggest and Copy fill the draft. Apply is one `ChangeTool` undo step. The row of the document material is marked.\n\nChangelog row: A Recipes tab shows a tool's speeds and feeds per material, with surface speed and feed per tooth, and can suggest or copy them.\n",
